WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.816
<v Mishu>Hello! Today I'm taking you on a trip through time. But first, a puzzle.

00:00:08.816 --> 00:00:10.925
<v Rohan>A puzzle? I love puzzles!

00:00:10.925 --> 00:00:13.857
<v Mother>Bhaiya, please make it longer. Char angula.

00:00:13.857 --> 00:00:17.766
<v Ishita>Char angula? That's four fingers. Easy!

00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:23.780
<v Mishu>Four fingers longer. But whose four fingers? Hers? The tailor's? Or yours?

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.770
<v Rohan>Hmm. My fingers are much thinner than my dad's.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.272
<v Mishu>An angula is the width of a finger.

00:00:29.172 --> 00:00:36.324
<v Mishu>People in India have measured with it for thousands of years, and tailors and carpenters still use it today.

00:00:36.324 --> 00:00:39.438
<v Ishita>Then every tailor would get a different answer!

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:44.665
<v Mishu>Today, a tailor in Delhi and a tailor in Chennai measure the same cloth and get the same answer.

00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:49.008
<v Mishu>How did the whole world come to agree? Hold on tight. Our tour begins!

00:00:49.008 --> 00:00:49.955
<v Rohan>Let's go!
